    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d796">

                <pb facs="1206" n="1192" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg1192"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Korea/5–1048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Political Adviser in Korea</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jacobs</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-05-10">May 10, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>340. Cite Zpol 4969. Up to hour of preparation
                    this message (7 p. m., May 10) election in Seoul has passed off without
                    sufficient incidents to seriously affect election on large scale and reports
                    from provinces received so far indicate same thing. Total reported killed today
                    are 18 (5 police, 9 Communists and 4 Rightists). Even though this figure may
                    increase as reports come in, total casualties for 20 million people should be
                    comparatively light. Voting in Seoul was heavy, over 90% of registrants. Reports
                    from provinces also indicate heavy vote. No reports received from Cheju
                    Island.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jacobs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
